  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the maximum and minimum outcomes, preferring the lottery with the more favorable maximum outcome (here, 4000€ vs. 3000€), and only if those are equal, then the minimum. The individual, however, does not consider the monetary outcomes at all in their reasoning. Instead, they base their decision solely on the probability of winning 3000€. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason, which is based on outcome comparisons. The information considered (probabilities) is different from what the reason requires (outcomes). The justification (higher chance of a smaller gain) does not match the rule of the reason (prefer higher maximum outcome). Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
