{
  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates lotteries based on their maximum and minimum outcomes. It prefers the lottery with the more favorable maximum outcome; if those are equal, it then considers the minimum outcome. In this case, both lotteries have a maximum outcome of 6000 Euros (B) and 3000 Euros (A), so the maximum outcomes are not equal. Therefore, the reason would prefer Lottery B because it has the higher maximum outcome (6000 vs. 3000). The minimum outcome for both lotteries is 0 Euros, so that part is equal. Thus, the decision reason clearly applies and would select B.",
